<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch3-chapter-first-eda" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Exploring Data</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter will introduce students to more big ideas that they will learn throughout the course, 
        but this chapter is focused more on the data visualization step of a statistical investigation and more
        generally on - interrogating data (with some ethics thrown in), getting comfortable with the omnipresence of variability in data, 
        and on multivariable thinking. This is mainly introduced through a full data exploration of a large data set.</p>
  </introduction>

